00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.670 align:start position:0%
 
hey what's up this doctor john delaney  with ramsey network  today we're going to be talking about  how do you choose to not let things  bother you i got a great email from josh  let's jump into it  josh writes thank you dr d for what  you've been doing brother you're welcome  your wisdom and guidance has helped me  at a time when i've been at one of my  lowest points  man that sucks i'm sorry to hear that  we're thinking about you man and i hope  you're doing well by the time this video  comes out  i still have some work to do but i've  heard you talk a lot about  choosing to not let things bother you  any advice on that  i don't know how to go about just  choosing to not let things get to me  sometimes  thank you for everything josh i love  this question thank you so  much for reaching out here's the deal we  live in a culture that is obsessed with  outsourcing its feelings its thoughts  its actions its responsibilities  everything is always somebody else's  fault  i'm always doing this because she made  me  cuz i have adhd because i was anxious  because i was angry because of something  that happened to me a long time ago it's  just the way our culture works these  days  it's pretty lame we live in a not my  fault society if you want to live a  healthier more productive  more joyful more laughter filled life  with lower stress fewer health problems  not die of a heart attack at 42 less  anger fewer  broken cracked up relationships you can  choose  to not let things bother you or better  yet you can choose to let only a few  things bother you  the few things that matter the few  things that you want to get on a hill  and die  on and the rest of everything else you  can let  roll off as the great jay-z says just  brush your shoulders off right here's a  good example  this weekend my son and i were going  somewhere we were taking my old pickup  truck  i had a big mason jar filled with water  and i set it on top of the cup holder in  the truck  it doesn't fit all the way down so just  resting on top  i'm always talking to my son about how  he smashes through  doors and is always stomping on things  and he just  ping-pongs his way through life he's  like a walking pinball machine right  a giant elephant in a bathroom of sorts  i set this glass of water down my son  gets into the truck he opens the door  slams it jumps in and goes hello  dad and as he did that that water fell  down  dumped the entire jar of water into my  floorboard  and then rolled out of the truck because  i had my door open rolls out of the  truck and smashes  into a bajillion pieces on the driveway  all in one like quick one  second little smash  and instantly i got mad like i felt it  rise up  and then instantly i just exhaled it out  and i looked over at him and said hey  let's get that cleaned up  and i saw him drop his head because he  knows that we're always talking about  entering into a space calmly and with  respect you never know who's on the  other side of a door  i've talked to him about treating my  truck with dignity and not smashing  everything  and slamming doors i also taught him  about saying you're sorry when you hurt  somebody when you break something  and being a part of the solution so he  walked around the truck he helped me  pick up the glass  i looked at him and said we got the  message here and he said yes sir i'm  sorry  i'll be more careful getting in the  truck next time i said cool thanks  so here's the deal my son apologized  he learned a great experiential lesson  it's not just  all theoretical head knowledge he got to  see if he's not thoughtful if he's not  intentional and he's just flying through  life  knocking things over he can dump a jar  of water into somebody's floorboard  smash a glass on a sidewalk all on  accident  all without just thinking right so as a  dad i got my point across  i didn't lose my temper i didn't fly off  the handle i didn't get angry  i didn't give him things to talk about  in some future counseling session right  i chose not to let that bother me he  apologized he helped clean up the mess  he made it right we're moving on so now  we're back to you josh  how do you choose to not let things  bother you  how did i override my instant i'm  frustrated i'm angry  nah i'm gonna move on two words  you decide and you practice you decide  i don't want to be a person who flies  off the handle i don't want to be a  person who walks around life  angry clenched tensed up i don't want to  be a person who's  always looking for where i'm going to  get offended i don't want to be somebody  who's always looking for somebody to  cancel  somebody to permanently ruin over  something they said they got frustrated  they did  accidentally whatever i don't live like  that  i want to live peacefully i want to live  joyfully i want to spend more time  laughing than i do angry i want to spend  more time in relationship  than out of relationship i have to  decide that number one i got to make it  a priority  i got to make it a destination and  number two he's got to practice  i have to practice i've got to come up  with some alternative behaviors and i've  got to implore them  i've got to walk away sometimes i got to  go for a walk sometimes when i'm  exhausted i'm tired  and i'm about to fly off the handle i'll  look at my wife and say i need to go for  a walk from it i'll be back in a second  and she knows me well enough to know  that's my way of saying i love you i  don't want to say something stupid  and so i'm going to head off for a  second i'll be back right and she honors  that  or i'll tell my kids i need to take a  breath for a second  give me one minute i'll be right back  and i'll go in my room  i'll exhale and then i can enter back  into the situation those moments are  rare nowadays  they're rare but they're still there  right they're still there i still have  my default settings  and then i don't want to blow it over  time you practice and you learn to say  things like  ah they don't get a vote ah this isn't  worth hurting a relationship over  ah what am i really getting at here i  want my son to learn how to say i'm  sorry  and to fix his messes that he's uh that  he causes and i want him to quickly be a  part of the solution  when he breaks something that's not his  right i got all three of those things  there's a dad i won  most things aren't worth hurting my  family or causing generational traumas  or flying off the handle so you practice  and you practice and you practice  i've given people close to me permission  to call me out to say hey man you're  being a jerk dude chill out  or what is that about or hey john go  take a walk man  and i listen to him because i trust him  i've given him permission to speak into  my life  it's part of practicing and the more you  practice in short order you will notice  things just start rolling off your back  you'll find yourself not taking big deep  breaths and clenching your fist  you'll see somebody flip you off while  you're driving and you'll just smile  cause okay congratulations dude  i'm going about my day you'll find  yourself get angry and then shut your  shoulders  exhale move on you'll find yourself  going  hey nah you know what i mean  and your whole life will just slowly  slowly start to lift  you decide and practice decide and  practice  it's not some complex google like  what do you call an algorithm right it's  just a decision  i don't want to be like that anymore i'm  going to practice not being like that  anymore  you can control your thoughts and your  actions  and if you control your thoughts and  your actions your feelings your emotions  they'll come alongside  thanks again for the question josh good  luck practicing  good luck deciding you're going to live  a more peaceful joyful life  this is dr john delony with ramsay  solutions don't forget to subscribe  send this video to your buddies if  they're struggling and don't forget  if you want to be a part of the dr john  deloney show if you want to call in and  talk with me  live on the air email me at ask  john ramseysolutions.com leave your cell  number  and kelly or one of the other ramsey  solutions team members will be  in touch with you shortly take care

